WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.122
This query uses correlation to calculate a test-specific benchmark.

00:00:04.122 --> 00:00:09.232
For a Glucose row, the inner query calculates the average Glucose result.

00:00:09.232 --> 00:00:13.902
For a Cholesterol row, it calculates the average Cholesterol result.

00:00:13.902 --> 00:00:17.162
The outer test name changes the inner query.

00:00:17.162 --> 00:00:22.087
This is a powerful pattern when one global benchmark would not be meaningful.

00:00:22.087 --> 00:00:26.577
A correlated subquery refers to the current row of the outer query.

00:00:26.577 --> 00:00:31.897
Conceptually, the inner query is evaluated in relation to each outer row.

00:00:31.897 --> 00:00:37.477
That makes some business rules easy to express, but it can be expensive at scale.

00:00:37.477 --> 00:00:42.480
Compare a correlated formulation with a pre-aggregated join when performance matters.
